  - path: docs/architecture.html
    tier: T1
    action: updated
    distills: "Two statements the import falsified, each narrowed to what is now true - the ONE T1 edit this epic has needed so far, and the line W2's result predicted W4 would move. The seam diagram's caption said 'the control API is purely a subscriber and reader - it never mutates capture state'; it now says the API is a subscriber and reader that also INGESTS (HAR import inserts flows the proxy never saw, marked as imported, through the same ring rules) but never rewrites or reinterprets what the capture path recorded - which keeps the load-bearing half of the original claim (the capture path's record is authoritative and the API does not touch it) while dropping the half that is false. The invariant row 'Open CORS on loopback' said 'Read-only API bound to loopback'; it now says 'Loopback-bound API ... widened to the methods its mutating routes need', because read-only is what DEC-12's grant was justified on and the justification that actually holds is the bind address, not the absence of writes. Rule-bearing T1, so the commit carries Reviewed-By: key vuluu via cargo xtask mr commit."
